        <param>
          <type>const std::exception &amp;</type>
          <declname>error</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Tests whether an exception represents a busy database (pool exhaustion or timeout). </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>First checks for a <computeroutput><ref refid="classDatabaseBusy" kindref="compound">DatabaseBusy</ref></computeroutput> by dynamic type; otherwise performs a case-sensitive substring search of <computeroutput>what()</computeroutput> for &quot;timeout&quot;, &quot;pool&quot;, &quot;too many clients&quot; and &quot;connection&quot;. The message check is a heuristic used because callers catch exceptions as <computeroutput>std::exception</computeroutput>, where the specific Drogon type may not be available. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">error</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Exception to classify; need not outlive the call. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>True if the exception looks like a busy/timeout condition. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="warning"><para>&quot;connection&quot; is a broad match: an unrelated error whose message mentions a connection is classified as busy. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
